      "marker_number": 3,
      "notes": "The whole thing is footnote q:  Citation — Martial. lib. 11. epigram. 4 Quotation — the actual couplet (Et qui purpureis jam tertia nomina fastis / Iane, refers Nervæ) Historical gloss — explaining that Trajan was also called Nerva after adoption Supporting citation — Aelian's Tactics in Greek as proof  It's one continuous note, moving from source location to quoted evidence to interpretive argument. I was wrong to treat it as a separate unnumbered item — the verse and the Aelian discussion are all part of q's apparatus, building the chronological case about Martial's dating.",
      "page_id": "p0044",
      "review_status": "locked",
      "reviewer": "Paul Boys",
